module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.by_ref_primitive_over_a_generic_call_argument_infers_from_the_borrow

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data by_ref_primitive_over_a_generic_call_argument_infers_from_the_borrow: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "by_ref_primitive_over_a_generic_call_argument_infers_from_the_borrow" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the Rust emitter types a by-ref primitive's argument from the callee's declared parameter before borrowing it, so a generic call argument is emitted at its declared carrier and rustc has no borrowed parameter to infer the call's generics from",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a by-ref primitive over a generic call argument lets rustc infer the generic from the borrowed parameter** INVALID STATE: a type-correct .dag call to a primitive whose rt_function_registry row passes by reference (extdeps.languages.rust.emit rt_function_registry, passes_by_ref: true; first instance map_keys), whose argument is itself a call to a GENERIC declaration (first instance std.algebra fold_list). The emitter writes v1_rt::map_keys(&fold_list(..)): the generic call is borrowed without its type being fixed, so rustc infers fold_list's accumulator A from the borrowed parameter (&HashMap<K, V>) instead of from fold_list's own empty: argument (rc_empty_map, Rc<HashMap<K, V>>).",

    "HARM: E0308 mismatched types at a site the .dag type checker accepted, so the source compiler admits a program its own Rust target cannot build -- the family of gunbc.recurring_failure_mode accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target, at a construction that row does not name. Measured on gunbc#15164 at 47612d0cb20d: v2-bootstrap run 40968160998 refused EmittedCompilerBuildFailed at the emitted v2_compiler_occurrence_resolution_census.rs, expected HashMap<_, _>, found Rc<HashMap<_, _>>, with rustc's own note that the argument influences the return type of fold_list. The .dag was map_keys(m: fold_list(xs: .., empty: empty_map(), cons: ..)) in v2.compiler.occurrence_resolution_census occurrence_resolution_partial. It was latent on main because the call went through std.algebra map_support_keys, whose parameter fixed the type before the borrow; removing that wrapper exposed it.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the same call with the argument bound to a let first compiles (the bound name has a concrete Rc type and &Rc<HashMap> deref-coerces), and so does a by-ref primitive over a non-generic argument. So the class is the conjunction by-ref borrow + generic call argument, not map_keys and not fold_list. RED fixture: fixtures/fixture_closure_rustc/by_ref_primitive_generic_call_argument_probe.dag; control differing only in the let: fixtures/fixture_closure_rustc/by_ref_primitive_bound_argument_probe.dag. Consumer: v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host fixture_closure_rustc_verdict. The pair is NOT enrolled on the merge path (gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path), so it executes on demand only and is not cited as rung 2. MEASURED 2026-10-30 (wise-moth-707): on srv1 at 47612d0cb20d, in an isolated clone, the opt-in v1-compiler lib test fixture_closure_rustc_discrimination was run with its green and red paths pointed, in an uncommitted local edit, at this control and this red; it passed (1 test, 204.75s), which by its assertions means the control's emitted crate compiled and rustc refused the red's with E0308 attributed to the red's own emitted module.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the refusal is loud and located at cargo on the required v2-bootstrap path, but nothing in acceptance reports it. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- the emitter has the callee's declared parameter type at the call site, so it can emit the argument at that carrier (or bind it) before borrowing; then no accepted program reaches this E0308. Not structurally impossible: the source can still write the shape, and the guarantee is the emitter's. NEXT TRIGGER is the capability named in trigger_capability; owner of the repair: the emission lane (clever-crane-830, routed by tidy-ant-251 2026-10-30).",

    "WORKAROUND SITES, which the repair must find and unwind: v2.compiler.occurrence_resolution_census occurrence_resolution_partial binds duplicate_set before map_keys and cites this row's symbol at that let. When the trigger lands, delete that let, keep the RED fixture as a permanent regression control, and flip the pair's expectation (DESIGN 4b(4)).",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_resolution_census", decl_name: "occurrence_resolution_partial", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "map_keys", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.algebra", decl_name: "fold_list", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target", decl_name: "accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
